An indie game done right.
Pros:
+ Excellent soundtrack;
+ Great narrating;
+ Weapons and weapon upgrades motivate different combat tactics;
+ Colorful and interestingly presented world;
+ Challenging towards the end (plus for me).
Cons:
- Lack of enemy variety;
- Even though there are many weapons and upgrades only a few become effective in later enemy encounters;
- Lacking end-game bosses;
- Could have included a few more puzzles.
By all means, try this game. It is worth playing just for the narrating and soundtrack.

The game itself is quite good and fun even, but it has several problems:
- Matchmaking is not yet balanced yet, but its early too be;
- Pay to win affects some of the fun, i don't think anyone likes running into a full golden gear dude in their 1st game and get completly destroyed;
- I dont like the fact that you have 3 free characters(Ranger, Barbarian and mage) and 3 paid ones(which you can buy with friend points, or even real money), it would help if you could buy them with gold or even BG).
But overall, its a great game, if they do the right moves.
Try it yourself.

